      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Cloud Spreadsheets","whyItMatters":"Google Sheets is a free, browser-based spreadsheet that eliminates local file management and enables instant team collaboration.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nGoogle Sheets is Google's cloud-native spreadsheet application. Unlike Excel, Sheets runs entirely in the browser — no installation needed. Files are saved automatically to Google Drive and can be accessed from any device.\n\n**Cloud Advantages:**\n- Auto-save after every keystroke\n- 100+ people can edit simultaneously\n- Changes sync in real time\n- Built-in revision history for 30 days\n\n```text\nGoogle Sheets vs Excel:\nAuto-save: Yes (continuous)\nCollaboration: Real-time multi-user\nPlatform: Browser, Android, iOS\nOffline: Available with Chrome extension\nVersion History: 30 days with named versions\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Sheets is free for personal use and included with Google Workspace\n- No local files — everything lives in the cloud\n- Collaboration is built-in, not an add-on","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"First Sheet","description":"Create your first Google Sheet","code":{"google-sheets":"// Open https://sheets.new in any browser\n// Sheets.new auto-creates a blank spreadsheet\n// Type in cell A1: 'Hello Google Sheets!'\n// Share via the blue Share button (top-right)"},"explanation":"sheets.new is a handy shortcut that creates a new blank spreadsheet instantly."}]}],
