      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Interface Overview","whyItMatters":"The Sheets interface is your workspace. Mastering the toolbar, menus, formula bar, and sheet tabs lets you navigate and use the application efficiently.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nThe Google Sheets interface is designed for productivity. Key components include:\n\n**Menu Bar:** File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Data, Tools, Extensions, Help\n\n**Toolbar:** Shortcut buttons for common actions — bold, italic, merge, currency format, alignment, colors, borders\n\n**Formula Bar:** Shows cell content; type `=` to start any formula. The name box at left shows the active cell reference.\n\n**Sheet Tabs:** Bottom tab bar lets you add (+), rename (double-click), reorder (drag), and color-code sheets.\n\n```text\nInterface Layout:\n[Menu Bar] [Toolbar]\n[Name Box] [Formula Bar]\n[Column Headers: A, B, C, D...]\n[Row Numbers: 1, 2, 3...]\n[Grid Area]\n[Sheet1 | Sheet2 | Sheet3] [+]\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Formula bar is essential for viewing and editing long formulas\n- Right-click sheet tabs for rename, duplicate, delete, hide\n- Customize toolbar by clicking the three-dot menu at the end","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Navigate Interface","description":"Practice using the interface","code":{"google-sheets":"// Click the + at bottom-left to add a sheet\n// Double-click 'Sheet1' and rename to 'Data'\n// Right-click the tab and choose 'Duplicate'\n// Click the paint palette to color the tab"},"explanation":"Sheet tabs are customizable — rename, duplicate, reorder, and color-code them."}]}],
