      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Formatting for Clarity","whyItMatters":"Well-formatted spreadsheets are easier to read, look professional, and communicate data effectively. Proper number formatting also ensures correct calculations.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nFormatting in Sheets changes appearance without changing underlying values. Each cell has formatting properties for font, fill, borders, alignment, and number format.\n\n**Text Formatting:**\n- Bold/Italic/Strikethrough: Toolbar buttons or Ctrl+B/I\n- Font color and cell fill color\n- Horizontal alignment: Left, Center, Right\n- Vertical alignment: Top, Middle, Bottom\n- Text wrapping: Overflow, Wrap, Clip\n\n**Number Formatting:**\n\n```text\nValue      Format           Display\n1234.5     Currency ($)     $1,234.50\n1234.5     Number           1,234.50\n0.15       Percent          15.00%\n1/1/2024   Date             January 1, 2024\n0.5        Duration         12:00:00\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Format > Number lets you control decimal places\n- Merge cells via toolbar for headers\n- Use paint format tool (paint roller icon) to copy formatting","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Format a Table","description":"Apply formatting to a data table","code":{"google-sheets":"// Select header row and click Bold (Ctrl+B)\n// Select data column > Format > Number > Currency\n// Select cells > Fill color > Light blue\n// Select range > Format > Number > Custom > #,##0.00"},"explanation":"Apply bold to headers, currency format to financial data, and fill colors for visual structure."}]}],
