      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Real-Time Collaboration","whyItMatters":"Google Sheets' collaboration features are its biggest advantage over desktop spreadsheets. Multiple people can work simultaneously, see each other's changes in real time, and communicate via comments.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nThe Share button (top-right) opens sharing settings. You can share with specific people (by email) or create a shareable link.\n\n**Permission Levels:**\n- Viewer: Can only view, cannot edit or comment\n- Commenter: Can view and add comments\n- Editor: Can view, edit, comment, and share\n\n**Collaboration Features:**\n\n```text\nReal-time cursors:\n  Each editor has a color-coded cursor\n  Shows their name and active cell\n\nComments:\n  Select cell > Right-click > Comment\n  Use @mention to notify specific people\n  Resolve comments when addressed\n\nAction items:\n  Assign tasks within comments\n  Checkboxes for to-dos\n  Email notifications\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Set expiration dates for link sharing\n- Use 'Anyone with the link' for public sharing\n- Editors can transfer ownership to others","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Share a Sheet","description":"Practice sharing and permissions","code":{"google-sheets":"// Click blue Share button\n// Enter email: colleague@company.com\n// Choose role: Editor\n// Click Send\n// Or copy link for 'Anyone with link can view'"},"explanation":"Share with specific people by email or create a shareable link with controlled permissions."}]}],
