      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Undo Mistakes with Versions","whyItMatters":"Version history is your safety net. Any change can be undone, any deleted data can be recovered, and named versions let you mark important milestones.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nGoogle Sheets automatically saves a version every time a significant change is made, or roughly every 10 minutes. History is kept for 30 days (or longer for Workspace accounts).\n\n**Using Version History:**\n- File > Version history > See version history\n- Or press Ctrl+Alt+Shift+H\n- Right panel shows timestamps and editors\n- Click a version to see the sheet state at that time\n\n**Named Versions:**\n\n```text\nFile > Version history > Name current version\n\nExample named versions:\n  'Draft 1 - Initial Budget'\n  'After Review Meeting'\n  'Final Approved - Q4'\n\nNamed versions are pinned and never expire\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Restore a version by clicking it then 'Restore this version'\n- Named versions help you bookmark important states\n- Version history also shows which editor made each change","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Version Demo","description":"Use version history","code":{"google-sheets":"// Make some edits to cells\n// File > Version history > See version history\n// Click different timestamps to preview\n// Click 'Restore this version' to go back\n// Name current version for future reference"},"explanation":"Version history lets you view, compare, and restore any previous state of the spreadsheet."}]}],
