      id: "gs-11", number: 11, title: "Basic Math Formulas", subtitle: "SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT, MIN, MAX", difficulty: "Beginner", estimatedMinutes: 55, xpReward: 70, prerequisites: [], learningObjectives: ["Use SUM to total values","Calculate AVERAGE","Find MIN and MAX in datasets"], partLabel: "Part 2: Formulas and Functions",
      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Essential Aggregation Functions","whyItMatters":"SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT, MIN, and MAX are the most frequently used functions in Sheets. They form the basis of all data analysis, from simple budgets to complex reports.","content":"**Core Concepts:**\n\nAll formulas start with `=`. Functions are predefined formulas that accept arguments in parentheses.\n\n**Basic Functions:**\n\n```text\n=SUM(A1:A10)       // Total of all values\n=AVERAGE(B1:B10)   // Arithmetic mean\n=COUNT(C1:C10)     // Count numeric cells\n=COUNTA(D1:D10)    // Count non-empty cells\n=MIN(E1:E10)       // Smallest value\n=MAX(F1:F10)       // Largest value\n```\n\n**Practical Example:**\n\n```text\nSales Data:\nProduct   | Units Sold | Price | Revenue\nWidget A  | 150        | $12   | =B2*C2\nWidget B  | 200        | $15   | =B3*C3\nWidget C  | 175        | $10   | =B4*C4\n----------------------------------------\nTotal     | =SUM(B2:B4)|       | =SUM(D2:D4)\nAverage   | =AVERAGE(B2:B4)\n```\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- Use Ctrl+Shift+Enter for array formulas (or use ARRAYFORMULA)\n- Functions ignore empty cells and text automatically\n- Select a range and look at the status bar for quick SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Math Functions","description":"Practice basic math functions","code":{"google-sheets":"=SUM(A2:A100)\n=AVERAGE(B2:B100)\n=COUNT(C2:C100)\n=MIN(D2:D100)\n=MAX(E2:E100)\n\n// Combined:\n=\"Total: $\"&TEXT(SUM(F2:F100),\"#,##0.00\")"},"explanation":"These five functions handle 80% of spreadsheet calculations. Master them first."}]}],
