      sections: [{"id":"s1","title":"Final Mastery Project","whyItMatters":"This chapter consolidates everything you've learned. You'll build a complete business intelligence system that demonstrates data analysis, automation, visualization, and script capabilities.","content":"**Mastery Project: Executive BI Dashboard**\n\nBuild a complete business intelligence system that combines all skills:\n\n**1. Data Layer:**\n- Import sales data from CSV or Google Forms\n- Clean data with TRIM, UNIQUE, SPLIT\n- Store in structured tables with named ranges\n\n**2. Analysis Layer:**\n- Pivot tables for monthly/quarterly trends\n- QUERY for dynamic analysis views\n- SUMIFS, COUNTIFS for conditional metrics\n- FORECAST for sales predictions\n\n**3. Visualization Layer:**\n- Line chart: Revenue trend with forecast\n- Bar chart: Performance by category\n- Pie chart: Market share breakdown\n- Scorecards with SPARKLINE for KPIs\n- Slicers for interactive filtering\n\n**4. Automation Layer:**\n- Custom menu: \"Refresh Data\" button\n- Time trigger: Daily data refresh\n- onEdit trigger: Auto-log changes\n- Custom functions: =CATEGORIZE() for segmenting\n\n**5. Collaboration Layer:**\n- Named versions for milestones\n- Comment threads for review\n- Action items for approvals\n- Scheduled email reports to executives\n\n**Review Checklist:**\n\n| Skill | Chapter |\n|-------|---------|\n| Navigation and Interface | 1-4 |\n| Data Entry and Formatting | 5-6 |\n| Named Ranges | 7 |\n| Sorting and Filtering | 8 |\n| Sharing and Collaboration | 9-10 |\n| Basic Functions (SUM, AVERAGE, etc.) | 11 |\n| Text, Logical, Date Functions | 12-14 |\n| Lookups (VLOOKUP, XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH) | 15-16 |\n| FILTER, QUERY, ARRAYFORMULA | 17-19 |\n| COUNTIF, SUMIF, Statistics, Finance | 20-22 |\n| Nested Formulas, Debugging | 23-24 |\n| Pivot Tables | 25 |\n| Charts (Bar, Line, Pie, Scatter, Area) | 26-30 |\n| Conditional Formatting, Data Validation | 31-32 |\n| Filters, Slicers, Sparklines | 33-34 |\n| Forecasting, Data Cleaning | 35-36 |\n| Apps Script, Automation | 37-48 |\n| Business Projects | 49-55 |\n| AI, Enterprise, Collaboration | 56-59 |\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n- A Google Sheets master combines formulas, data analysis, visualization, and automation\n- Real-world value comes from applying these skills to business problems\n- Keep learning — new Sheets features are released regularly","codeExamples":[{"id":"ex1","title":"Mastery Project","description":"Comprehensive Sheets demo","code":{"google-sheets":"// You've mastered:\n// =SUM(), =VLOOKUP(), =QUERY(), =ARRAYFORMULA()\n// Pivot Tables, Charts, Sparklines\n// Apps Script, Triggers, Custom Functions\n// Data Analysis, Forecasting, Automation\n\n// Final project: Executive BI Dashboard\n// Combines all skills into one solution\n\n\"Your Google Sheets journey is complete!\"\n\"You can now: Analyze data, automate workflows,\"\n\"build dashboards, and create business solutions.\""},"explanation":"Demonstrate complete Google Sheets mastery by building a comprehensive BI dashboard that uses everything from basic formulas to advanced automation."}]}],
